# Required by verify_v032_benchmarks.py / check_paper_artifact_consistency.py /
# export_week8_results.py: the v0.3.2 ablation, CV, scaffold-split and target-
# scaffold artifacts the frozen benchmarks and the paper tables recompute from.
# Without these negations every fresh checkout silently lacks them (a tracked
# sibling such as dielectric_v03_representation_ablation_predictions.csv is the
# same size class), so the CI gate failed on a clean clone.
!data/processed/v032_ablation_predictions.csv
!data/processed/v032_ablation_repeats.csv
!data/processed/v032_ablation_cv.csv
!data/processed/v032_scaffold_folds.csv
!data/processed/v032_target_scaffold_predictions.csv
!data/processed/v032_target_scaffold_metrics.csv
# Week 8 export artefacts: export_week8_results.py copies these two MLP
# calibration files into the delivery package, so a clean clone needs them.
!data/processed/dielectric_mlp_calibration_predictions.csv
!data/processed/dielectric_mlp_calibration_repeats.csv
!data/processed/nbs514_alpha_harmonization.csv
!data/processed/nbs514_alpha_internal_validation.csv
!data/processed/thermoml_local_coverage.csv
# v1.x temperature-resolved observation table: the builder, its verifier and
# the grouped-CV probe all read this file, so a clean clone needs it.
!data/processed/dielectric_observations_v11.csv
# W13 OpenAlex/Unpaywall sweep: the round-6 report cites this candidate list,
# so a clean clone needs it too.
!data/processed/openalex_oa_candidates.csv
# W13 AL Round 3 refresh queue: the candidate list is cited by its report.
!data/processed/al_round3_candidates.csv
# v1.x frequency-gate probe and ILThermo structure resolution: both probes
# and their reports read these tables, so a clean clone needs them.
!data/processed/dielectric_lowfreq_candidates.csv
!data/processed/ilthermo_new_compounds.csv
!data/processed/dielectric_lowfreq_structures.csv
# v1.x merged observation table (zero-frequency + admission-gated low-frequency
# rows) and the extra xTB feature block the coverage benchmark reads.
!data/processed/dielectric_observations_v11plus.csv
!data/processed/dielectric_physical_features_v11plus_new.csv
# The alpha-prior probe's fold-level predictions table is provenance-only: no test,
# verifier or delivery package reads the repository copy (the probe writes its own
# copy into the temp dir it is given), and at ~14 MB it is the largest single
# artefact of the round.  Its folds/repeats/crosscheck siblings stay tracked.
probes/artifacts/dielectric_alpha_prior_predictions.csv

# Outlet-2 LightGBM weights: ~72 MB of regenerable binaries.  Nothing in the
# test suite reads them (test_export_week13_results.py only asserts they are
# absent from the delivery bundle), and models/homo_lumo_baselines.json already
# pins each file's sha256, so the provenance survives without the bytes.
models/*.ubj

*.zip
*.xml
*.pdf

# API keys
config/

# G1+ source-priority pass: raw fetch caches live under data/external/g1plus/
# and are regenerated by re-running the collectors.  They are not committed -
# in particular not the text extraction of the closed-access Wiley supplement.
# Durable evidence is kept in probes/g1plus_*.json and reports/g1plus_*.md.
data/external/g1plus/
